  "answer": "I don't have a shell tool available to execute tests, so I'll verify the logic by tracing through the public test cases manually:\n\n**Test 1:** `parseTags('red,blue,green')`\n- `'red'` → trim → `'red'`, no whitespace runs, lowercase → `'red'` ✓\n- `'blue'` → `'blue'` ✓\n- `'green'` → `'green'` ✓\n- Result: `['red', 'blue', 'green']` ✓\n\n**Test 2:** `parseTags('  Red , , BLUE  ,')`\n- `'  Red '` → trim → `'Red'` → lowercase → `'red'` ✓\n- `' '` → trim → `''` → discarded ✓\n- `' BLUE  '` → trim → `'BLUE'` → lowercase → `'blue'` ✓\n- `''` → discarded ✓\n- Result: `['red', 'blue']` ✓\n\n**Test 3:** `parseTags('Alpha,beta,alpha,BETA,gamma')`\n- `'Alpha'` → `'alpha'` (new) ✓\n- `'beta'` → `'beta'` (new) ✓\n- `'alpha'` → `'alpha'` (dup, skipped) ✓\n- `'BETA'` → `'beta'` (dup, skipped) ✓\n- `'gamma'` → `'gamma'` (new) ✓\n- Result: `['alpha', 'beta', 'gamma']` ✓\n\n**Edge cases:**\n- `parseTags('')` → `''.split(',')` = `['']` → normalized `''` → discarded → `[]` ✓\n- `parseTags(',,,')` → all empty → `[]` ✓\n- Non-string input → `TypeError` ✓\n- Internal whitespace collapse: `'a\\t\\tb'` → `'a b'` ✓ (uses `\\s+` which matches JS whitespace runs)\n- Case-sensitive dedup after normalization: since we lowercase before comparing, differently-cased spellings collapse to the same key and count as duplicates ✓\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `parseTags(input)` in `tags.mjs`, keeping the named export and leaving `public.test.mjs` untouched.\n\n**Implementation details:**\n- **Type guard:** throws `TypeError` if `input` is not a string.\n- **Split:** uses `input.split(',')` — splits only on literal commas.\n- **Normalization per part:** `.trim()` (surrounding JS whitespace) → `.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ')` (collapse each nonempty internal whitespace run to one ASCII space) → `.toLowerCase()`.\n- **Discard empties:** skips parts that normalize to `''`.\n- **Dedup:** a `Set` tracks normalized tags, so differently-cased spellings of one tag (which normalize to the same string) count as duplicates; first-occurrence order is preserved via the `result` array.\n- **Empty/delimiter-only input:** returns `[]`.\n\nAll three public tests pass by manual trace, and the edge cases (empty string, delimiter-only, non-string input, internal whitespace) behave as specified.",
